[agent:result] 156	## Data API
[agent:result] 157	
[agent:result] 158	PostgREST-compatible HTTP API for CRUD operations on Postgres tables. **Autoscaling only.**
[agent:result] 159	
[agent:result] 160	### Enabling
[agent:result] 161	
[agent:result] 162	1. Navigate to **Data API** in the Lakebase project UI
[agent:result] 163	2. Click **Enable Data API** — auto-creates the `authenticator` role and `pgrst` schema
[agent:result] 164	3. The `public` schema is exposed by default
[agent:result] 165	
[agent:result] 166	### Authentication
[agent:result] 167	
[agent:result] 168	All requests require a Databricks OAuth bearer token:
[agent:result] 169	
[agent:result] 170	```
[agent:result] 171	Authorization: Bearer <databricks-oauth-token>
[agent:result] 172	```
[agent:result] 173	
[agent:result] 174	Each Databricks identity must have a matching Postgres role — the auto-created `authenticator` role assumes the caller's identity at query time.
[agent:result] 175	
[agent:result] 176	**Create a role for Data API access:**
[agent:result] 177	
[agent:result] 178	```sql
[agent:result] 179	CREATE ROLE "user@example.com" LOGIN;
[agent:result] 180	GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA public TO "user@example.com";
[agent:result] 181	GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public TO "user@example.com";
[agent:result] 182	```
[agent:result] 183	
[agent:result] 184	### CRUD Operations
[agent:result] 185	
[agent:result] 186	```bash
[agent:result] 187	# GET — query with filters, pagination, ordering
[agent:result] 188	curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" "$DATA_API_URL/public/users?age=gt.21&limit=10&order=created_at.desc"
[agent:result] 189	
[agent:result] 190	# POST — insert
[agent:result] 191	curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
[agent:result] 192	  -d '{"name": "Alice", "email": "alice@example.com"}' "$DATA_API_URL/public/users"
[agent:result] 193	
[agent:result] 194	# PATCH — update (filter required)
[agent:result] 195	curl -X PATCH -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
[agent:result] 196	  -d '{"status": "inactive"}' "$DATA_API_URL/public/users?id=eq.42"
[agent:result] 197	
[agent:result] 198	# DELETE (filter required)
[agent:result] 199	curl -X DELETE -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" "$DATA_API_URL/public/users?id=eq.42"
[agent:result] 200	```
[agent:result] 201	
[agent:result] 202	### Row-Level Security (RLS)
[agent:result] 203	
[agent:result] 204	Strongly recommended for multi-tenant data. Policies use `current_user` (the authenticated Databricks email).
[agent:result] 205	
[agent:result] 206	```sql
[agent:result] 207	ALTER TABLE users ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
[agent:result] 208	CREATE POLICY user_isolation ON users USING (email = current_user);
[agent:result] 209	```
[agent:result] 210	
[agent:result] 211	### Configuration
[agent:result] 212	
[agent:result] 213	Via the Data API UI: exposed schemas, max rows, CORS origins, OpenAPI spec.
[agent:result] 214	
[agent:result] 215	### Unsupported PostgREST Features
[agent:result] 216	
[agent:result] 217	Computed relationships, inner-join embedding, custom media type handlers, stripped-nulls, planned/estimated counts, transaction control via headers, EXPLAIN/trace, pre-request functions, GUCs, PostGIS auto-GeoJSON.
[agent] The Lakebase Data API needs UI enablement + curl (blocked) + psql (missing), so it's not viable CLI-only. The robust online read path here is **Online Table + Feature Serving endpoint**, queried via `serving-endpoints query`. The feature-spec creation needs the feature-engineering library, which I'll run **on the platform** via a notebook job (orchestrated by the CLI). Let me reset cwd and start building.
